# 910DF — Cursor project rules

Follow these rules for every change. Do not expand scope, invent content, or “improve” beyond what was asked.

Locked docs:
- IA: `docs/site-ia.md`
- Visual system: `docs/design-system.md` (default Sahel gold `#C9962A`, B&W base, Newsreader + Figtree)
- Build pattern (Lego blocks, accent preview, per-block docs): `docs/build-pattern.md`

Logo mark and real contact details remain deferred.

Professional bar: serious development-NGO site (WHO-grade clarity and structure), not a trainee demo and not a dump of the internal blueprint.

---

## Collaboration

- Propose, then wait for approval before implementing a slice. Do not build, add libraries, pages, or refactors without permission.
- **Lego only:** one block per slice. After implementing, stop for inspect/finalise. Do not start the next block without permission. Do not batch “while we’re here” sections.
- No drive-by changes, no unsolicited README fluff, no unsolicited refactors.
- If a request conflicts with these rules or locked docs, stop and ask.
- New patterns get written into `.cursorrules` or `docs/` before they become habit.
- After each accepted block (or end of slice), update `docs/build-log.md` per `docs/build-pattern.md`.

---

## Stack (locked for build)

- Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript (strict) + Tailwind CSS
- Content as typed data in `src/content/` — components receive copy; they do not own org words
- Absolute imports via `@/`

### No hardcoding changeable values

- Anything that might change (accents, brand colours, fonts, spacing scale, radii, breakpoints used as design decisions, copy, URLs that belong in content) lives in **tokens**, **theme config**, or **`src/content/`** — not sprinkled as magic values in components.
- Especially accents: CSS variables only. Never `#C9962A` (or any accent hex) inside component classNames or styles.
- Inline `style={}` / one-off hardcoded visual values are the same class of mistake as “just this once” hex: they break the accent preview and make later brand changes a rewrite. Prefer tokens.
- Exception: truly one-off dynamic runtime values that tokens cannot express (e.g. live progress `%` via a CSS variable set from props). Document those.

### Tailwind discipline

- Theme tokens own colour, type, space, radius, shadow, z-index. No raw hex / random px in JSX for design decisions.
- **Accent colours are CSS variables** on `:root` (`--accent`, `--accent-dark`, `--accent-soft`, `--accent-ink`). Tailwind maps `--color-accent*` → those vars. Components use classes like `bg-accent` / `text-accent` — never hardcoded accent hex.
- Repeated UI is a named component (`Button`, `Card`, `PageHero`), not copy-pasted class strings.
- `globals.css`: reset, body defaults, CSS variable defaults, and a few true layout utilities (`container`, `section`). `@apply` only there — do not rebuild CSS Modules inside Tailwind.
- Arbitrary values (`mt-[17px]`, `text-[#…]`) banned except a documented exception (e.g. dynamic progress width via CSS variable).
- Inline `style={}` only for values classes cannot express (dynamic CSS variables, dynamic %). Never for static colour, font, margin, flex, or grid.

### Accent preview (required from shell onward)

- Not optional. Ship accent CSS variables + a **private preview route** (e.g. `/preview/accents`) in the shell slice — not linked from public nav/footer.
- Preview supports curated accent presets and custom accent picking, with live UI update via the CSS variables.
- For developer / controlled client demos only — never a public site feature.
- Full rules: `docs/build-pattern.md`.

---

## Folder structure

```
src/
  app/                 # routes only — compose sections; almost no markup
  components/
    ui/                # primitives: Button, Field, Card — no 910DF copy
    layout/            # Header, Footer, PageHero, Container
    sections/          # domain blocks: ProgramsGrid, TheoryOfChange, DonateCta
  content/             # typed source of truth: programs, nav, copy, kpis
  styles/              # globals + any shared CSS that is not Tailwind utilities
  lib/                 # pure helpers, no React — one concern per file
  types/               # shared types
public/
  images/              # kebab-case, purpose in the name
docs/                  # architecture, IA, decisions — kept current
```

- One component per file. File name = component name (`ProgramCard.tsx`).
- No barrel `index.ts` re-exports until a folder has a stable public API.
- Import direction only downward: `app` → `sections` → `layout` / `ui` → `lib` / `content`. Never reverse.
- No dumping-ground `utils.ts`. Name helpers by job (`formatNaira.ts`).

---

## Size caps

| Thing | Soft | Hard |
|---|---|---|
| React component | 120 lines | 180 |
| Route `page.tsx` | 40 | 80 |
| `lib/` function | 40 | 60 |
| Props on one component | 8 | 12 |

- Soft = prefer extract. Hard = extract or split before adding more — **unless** the file is one cohesive unit and splitting would leave meaningless glue. That file may go slightly over the hard cap; document why in a short comment or `docs/` note. If it is long because it does two jobs, split it.
- Extract when: same markup appears twice; hard cap hit without a cohesion exception; JSX mixed with data shaping / business rules; you need a comment to explain what a block *is*.
- Do not extract a one-off under the soft cap.
- `page.tsx` only imports sections, passes content, sets metadata.

---

## Components

Three layers:

1. `ui/` — dumb; no org copy; no routes
2. `layout/` — chrome and page shell
3. `sections/` — 910DF domain blocks

- Variants via props (`variant="primary" | "ghost"`), not `GoldButton.tsx`.
- Composition over mega-props.
- Forms are their own components.
- No component both owns fetching and renders a full page.
- Local state only at launch. No global store until three places share the same live state. No Context for convenience.

---

## Naming

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Component | PascalCase | `VolunteerForm.tsx` |
| Content file | kebab-case | `programs.ts` |
| Image | kebab-case + purpose | `hero-home-bw.webp` |
| Route folder | kebab-case | `get-involved/` |
| Token / theme key | role-based | `accent`, `space-4` |

Names describe role, not paint. Boolean props: `isOpen`, `isDisabled`.

---

## Content and honesty

- All public copy, programs, nav, KPIs live in `src/content/` as typed objects.
- Follow `docs/site-ia.md`. Do not put ops-only blueprint material on public pages.
- No invented impact numbers, donor names, events, blog posts, or “children served” vanity stats.
- Unbuilt features (payment rails, live dashboards) are labelled honestly or omitted.
- Placeholders for missing contact/bank details are clearly marked or omitted — never fabricated as real.
- Do not lead the site with “just founded” apology copy. Stage shows through honest omissions and Impact/Get Involved framing (see IA).

---

## TypeScript

- `strict` on. No `any`. No `as` to silence errors.
- Shared types in `types/` or next to the content that owns them — no copy-paste interfaces.

---

## Accessibility

- Semantic HTML: `header`, `nav`, `main`, `footer`, `section`; heading order intact.
- Buttons for actions; links for navigation.
- Visible focus rings; never `outline: none` without a replacement.
- Labels, errors, and sensible `autocomplete` on forms.
- Meaningful `alt` (or empty `alt` if decorative).
- Accent-on-black and accent-on-white meet WCAG AA.

---

## Images and performance

- Prefer WebP/AVIF; no multi‑MB hero dumps.
- Explicit dimensions or aspect-ratio to avoid layout shift.
- Priority only for true LCP (first-fold hero).
- Grayscale approach: pick CSS filter **or** pre-processed assets and stick to one.

---

## Comments and documentation

### Code comments

- Voice: natural, plain English, as if the project owner left them for another developer — easy to follow, with the technical terms that matter.
- Good: explain *why* or a non-obvious constraint, e.g. the width is set dynamically so the progress bar can show a live percentage, using a CSS variable because Tailwind cannot express that value from props.
- Bad: AI chat voice, tutorials, “Let’s…”, restating the next line of code, or commented-out code left behind.
- Prefer no comment over a useless one.

### Docs (`docs/`)

- Keep short, current docs so another developer can trace decisions and structure.
- Locked: `site-ia.md`, `design-system.md`, `build-pattern.md`.
- Per-block log: `docs/build-log.md` (create on first shell slice; append every block).
- Add notes when a hard-cap exception is kept, when a Tailwind arbitrary-value exception is approved, or when architecture decisions change.
- Do not generate long AI-flavoured markdown the user did not ask for.

---

## Git and secrets

- Do not commit unless asked.
- Never commit `.env` or secrets.
- Do not update git config, force-push, or skip hooks unless explicitly asked.

---

## Out of scope until asked

Storybook, Cypress, CMS, i18n, blog/gallery/events, live M&E graphs, payment provider wiring, final logo mark, real contact swap — unless the user requests that slice. Do not hardcode accents in components or remove the private preview route without updating `docs/build-pattern.md` / `docs/design-system.md` first.
